Disable EnsureIncluded's rewrite of the root Hyprland config.

hyprmoncfg appends/moves a `dofile(...)`/`source = ...` line in the root
Hyprland config (hyprland.lua/hyprland.conf) via WriteFileAtomic, which does
a write-temp-then-rename. rename(2) replaces whatever sits at that path,
including a symlink -- so when the root config is a symlink managed by an
external tool (e.g. Nix Home Manager), hyprmoncfg silently replaces the
symlink with a plain file it owns. This fights with Home Manager's
activation, which expects to own that symlink.

This patch disables the rewrite for now: EnsureIncluded becomes a no-op that
reports the include line without ever touching the root config file. The
include/source line must be added to the root Hyprland config manually (and
kept there statically) instead of being managed by hyprmoncfg.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/crmne/hyprmoncfg (not yet filed)

